@@ -9,6 +9,22 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Visited view cache
+
+The shared layout preserves the five most recently visited page views in a
+container managed by Astro's client router. Returning to a cached route reuses
+its DOM and hydrated component state. Inactive views use `content-visibility:
+hidden`, `inert`, and `aria-hidden`; older views are evicted to bound memory use.
+Browsers without `content-visibility` use `display: none` as a fallback.
+
+Cache keys include the pathname and query string, while fragments share a view.
+Navigating to the current route again refreshes its DOM. Astro still fetches each
+destination and manages the page head, browser history, and scroll restoration;
+the cache saves rebuilding page content, not network requests. Cached content
+retains its previous state until it is refreshed, evicted, or the page reloads.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for automated DOM and router integration checks (Node 22.6+).
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
